{
  "name": "pairwise_advantage_gap_loss",
  "intuition": "This loss encourages selecting higher advantage pairs by penalizing lower advantage in the pair, reinforcing preference for higher advantage signals. Using advantage_gap as the core signal leverages the relative quality difference between pairs, which intuitively promotes learning from the most informative comparisons. Applying logsigmoid to advantage_gap enhances gradient stability for large differences.",
  "pseudocode": "loss = mean( logsigmoid( advantage_w - advantage_l ) * weight )",
